  "text": "Recipe: Adai\nCreator: Kumar Natarajan\nCategory: Pancake/Crepe\nIngredients: 1 cup brown rice, 3/4 cup each of toor dal, urad dal, moong dal, chana dal, 1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 tsp fennel seeds, 5 red chillies, 1/4 tsp hing (asafetida), 1 inch ginger, Salt to taste (~1 tsp), 1 red onion finely chopped, 2 cups of moringa leaves, Coriander if desired\nCooking methods: soak, blend, ferment, pan-fry\nInstructions: BATTER:\n+ SOAK & GRIND: Soak the rice and dals for 4-6 hours. Then rinse and transfer to a wet grinder or blender. Add hing, ginger, cumin & fennel. Add salt to taste. Grind to a coarse granularity batter, adding water as required.\n+ FERMENT: Batter may be fermented for 2 hours or consumed without fermentation.\n+ Add chopped onion, moringa leaves and coriander. Mix well.\nADAI:\n+ Heat a dosa pan and prepare adai similar to a dosa. It is made slightly thicker than a dosa.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (brown rice), BEANS (toor dal, urad dal, moong dal, chana dal), LEAFY GREENS (moringa leaves), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
